 ],
 "literal": "Palmyra palm tree of large stature with a trunk like a drum base, / in its nest of small twigs woven with thick palmyra fronds, / the black-legged anril bird's desirable, advanced pregnant / female bird with pregnancy cravings calls out at midnight, / cleaving through the village common ground, the tall chariot with a group of bells / even though it does not come, as if it is coming, / with the sound ringing inside my ears, / my eyes have indeed abandoned sleep, O friend!",
 "translation": "On the palmyra palm tree, which stands tall with a trunk as thick as a drum's base, inside a nest of small twigs woven with thick fronds, the black-legged female anril bird, heavy with advanced pregnancy and filled with longing, calls out at midnight. At this hour, even though his tall chariot with its cluster of bells does not come cleaving through the village common ground, my ears ring with that very sound as if he is arriving. Because of this, O friend, my eyes have completely abandoned sleep.",
 "modern": "முழவின் அடிப்பகுதி போன்ற தடித்த தண்டுடைய, பெரிய பனைமரத்தின் செழுமையான மடல்களாலும் சிறு குச்சிகளாலும் கட்டப்பட்ட கூட்டில், கரிய கால்களையுடைய அன்றில் பறவையின் ஆசையூட்டும் முதிர்ந்த சூலினைக் கொண்ட பெண் பறவை தன் கர்ப்ப வேட்கையால் நள்ளிரவில் கூவுகிறது. அந்த நள்ளிரவில், ஊர் மன்றத்தைக் கடந்து வரும் ஒலிக்கின்ற மணிகளைக் கொண்ட தலைவனின் நெடிய தேர் வராவிட்டாலும், அது வருவது போல என் காதுகளில் அந்த ஓசை ஒலிக்கிறது. அதனால், தோழியே! என் கண்கள் தூக்கத்தை முழுமையாகத் துறந்துவிட்டன.",
 "explanation": "The heroine is speaking to her close friend in a state of deep distress during the midnight hours. She describes a pregnant female anril bird crying out from its nest in a tall palmyra tree, an image that intensifies her own feelings of loneliness and longing. Although the hero's bell-adorned chariot has not actually arrived, she constantly imagines hearing its sound passing through the village common ground. This auditory illusion keeps her awake, causing her eyes to completely abandon sleep. The imagery of the nesting anril bird, traditionally known for its inseparable partnership, serves as a poignant contrast to the heroine's solitary waiting.",
 "model": "gemini-3.5-flash",
